## 2. The duplicate-embedding set — both audits, fully verified

Table columns: Token | Host A | Host B | Consensus owner
- `oodns-cloud` | `oomesh` | `oogateway` (3rd: own repo) | **`oomesh`** (RFC L6 mesh pairing); strip from `oogateway`
- `ooqueue` | `oodb-dist` | `oosched-cloud` | **`oodb-dist`** (queue = data plane; `oosched-cloud` is non-canonical anyway)
- `ooclip` | `oofiles` | `ooportal` | **`ooportal`** (capability-grant boundary is the honest owner)
- `ooshot` | `oofiles` | `ooportal` | **`ooportal`** (same)
- `ootaskmgr` | `oofiles` | `oocockpit` (itself a `oopanel` persona) | **`oopanel`** transitively — a persona cannot host a
  persona
- `ooarchitect` | `oogovern` (30-pg subtree, byte-identical to standalone) | `oooda-engine` (`persona/architect.oo` — rewritten
  variant that **drops `ooarch_basename`**) | **`oogovern`** — its copy preserves SSoT; retire engine's divergent variant
- `oohealthd` | `ooinit` (`healthd/` subtree, 8 pages) | standalone repo ships `bin/oohealthd` | **`oohealthd` repo** — it is in
  RFC's L2 canonical-8; strip `ooinit/healthd/` (see §4.4)
- `engine` (alias) | `oooda-engine` (`meta.oo:24`) | `ooherdr` (`meta.oo:34`) | one side drops it — recommend `ooherdr` keeps,
  `ooooda` loses on rename
- `sha256sum` (token) | `oohash` relay | `oob3sum` relay **+ `ooflash/digest.oo`** | digest host (§4.7); `ooflash` must go
  native anyway

