## 3. Unique findings (one auditor only)

### 3.1 mcode-only — spot-verified in this pass

Table columns: Finding | Evidence | Consensus adoption
- **`std/hw` kernel stack** — 112 impl `.oo` pages across 9 subdirs in a "standard library"; 2 verbatim-identical cap-space
  pages vs `ookernel-ob`; `std/anchor.oo` vs `std/hw/anchor.oo` self-contradict | M§2.1/§3.2. Verified: exactly 112 in subdirs
  (127 incl. top-level theory pages) | **SPLIT `std`→`std`+`std-hw`.** The largest single-scope violation in the fleet; devin
  missed it entirely (called L0 "cleanest org")
- **`oohash`↔`oob3sum` mutual persona cycle** | `oohash/ipc/dispatch_persona.oo:33` ↔ `oob3sum/ipc/persona_dispatch.oo:32` —
  verbatim | Critical — feeds §4.7
- **`ooimage` overclaim + port bug** — README:76 promises L1 ISO + L2 UEFI/Firecracker; only container-string gen exists;
  `ooda_inference.oo:24,28`=`11434` vs `:39`=`11435` | M§2.2/F6. Verified | RENAME `oocontainer`; fix port bug (a live
  functional defect)
- **`oovm-ui` overclaim** — README promises KVM VM manager; sole domain page is a 42-line `/proc/meminfo`+`loadavg` reader |
  M§2.7. Verified (zero qemu/kvm in domain code) | RENAME `oohostmon`
- **Hidden aliases**: `oocompctl`→`oocomp`, `oowallpaper`→`oowall`, `oonotify`→`ootoast`, `ooidle`/`ooscreensaver` self-absorbed
  by `oolock` | M§4.6 | Add to ownership table
- **`oodeepseek` vendor persona** inside `oocoder` + hardcoded `:11435` | M§2.13. Verified | RENAME `oocoder-deepseek`
- **`oodrv-net` overclaim** — promises e1000e/RTL8125; delivers a 7-word frame codec; own union persona already `oodrv-io` |
  M§2.10 | RENAME `oodrv-io`
- **`ookernel-hal-x86` overclaim** — x86-named host covering 3 archs | M§2.11 | RENAME `oohal`
- **`oooda-engine` stutter** | M§2.12 | RENAME `ooooda`
- **`bedaisy_gate` in `ookernel-mm`** — BattlEye/Destiny-2 anti-cheat IOMMU gate inside a memory manager; duplicated
  `ookernel-ob/nt/` | M§3.4. Verified header | Extract → `ookernel-ob/nt/` before archive
- **`oorouter` L6 files** (`core/fleet.oo`,`gpu_schedule.oo`) duplicating `ooinfer-grid` | M§3.5. Verified | Delete both files;
  fold remainder → `ooherdr`
- **`ooherdr` 4-domain split** — roster + cluster failover + `oomux` TUI + hardcoded vendor-driver registry | M§3.6. Verified |
  Extract `oomux` + registry
- **`lsp`/`mcp` ship-name debt** — `dist/mcp` vs `ooda-mcp`; 5-step legacy fallback `tui/mcp_client.oo:79`; `install.sh` puts
  bare `lsp`/`mcp` in `~/.openooda/bin` | M§2.8/§7.9/§7.10. Verified | Uniform `ooda-lsp`/`ooda-mcp`; retire bare names from
  install surface
- **`oodar` metadata contradictions** (lib name / layer / file-count) | M§2.9 | Doc fix
- **`oollama` anomaly** — only tools repo correctly absent from catalog; absorbed into `ooaid` | M§5.5. Verified | Archive repo;
  keep persona
- **Phantom `unix_consolidation_blueprint.md`** — directive cites a nonexistent doc | M§6.4. Verified absent | Fix directive →
  cite RFC 0012
- **README/AGENTS drift fleet-wide** — kernel page claims 10–16 vs actual 30–37; `95/95` vs `80` assertions; 11 agents repos one
  version behind; DE org profile says 20 lists 18, byte-identical stub ×20 | M§7.3/§7.4 | Doc sweep checklist
- **`oodac` 4 binary copies; kernel `SRC` omits `fs/fsprobe.oo` ×6; "ELF64 boot image" README lie ×6; `oodac_cluster.sh`
  fallback; `install.sh` 8-component surface** | M§7.5–7.10 | Hygiene + build-correctness
- **Hardcoded fleet hostnames/Tailscale IPs** — `status.oo:176-178` hard bindings; `fanout.oo:91`,`quota_ledger.oo:76-77`
  env-defaults; `ooaid` embeds hostnames in *identifiers* | M§7.8 (F12). Verified | Hard bindings must go; defaults documented;
  redaction table = declared exemption
- **Conformance sweep** — 246 core files >8 fns (worst `ai_multimodal.oo`=87); 1,857 fns >40 lines; duplicated 200-line
  `poly1305_mac` | M§8 | Declare shim exemption class + schedule cleanup; `boundary_257_lines.oo` needs allowlist entry
- **Negative-tested pairs** — `ooconsent`≠`ooconsensus`, `oostore`≠`oostore-cas`, `oobilling`/`ooquota`/`ootelemetry` distinct |
  M§2.18 | Good discipline; no action

